cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MethylForge, please cite it as below."
title: "MethylForge: a reproducible epigenome (DNA-methylation) analysis pipeline (methylation calls -> imprinting / episignature / DMR -> clinical & research reports)"
abstract: >-
  MethylForge is an organism- and disease-agnostic Nextflow DSL2 + Python pipeline
  for DNA-methylation (epigenome) analysis. It ingests short-read bisulfite/EM-seq,
  long-read native-5mC (Nanopore/PacBio), pre-called per-CpG methylation, or Illumina
  EPIC/450K array data, normalises everything to a single per-cytosine schema, and
  produces methylation QC, imprinted-DMR (imprinting-disorder) analysis, episignature
  classification, cohort DMP/DMR calling, and branded clinical/research reports. It is
  the epigenome counterpart to the CallForge germline-variant pipeline and emits a
  FamilyForge-compatible findings hand-off for downstream interpretation.
authors:
  - family-names: "Adu"
    given-names: "Bright"
    affiliation: "Genomics & Bioinformatics Core, Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research, University of Ghana, Legon, Ghana"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - DNA methylation
  - epigenome
  - bisulfite sequencing
  - nanopore
  - episignature
  - imprinting disorders
  - differential methylation
  - nextflow
references:
  - type: software
    title: "CallForge: a targeted-capture germline analysis pipeline"
    notes: "Sibling sequence-variant pipeline; MethylForge emits a FamilyForge-compatible findings hand-off that pairs with CallForge output."
  - type: software
    title: "FamilyForge: family-based variant interpretation and reporting"
    notes: "Downstream interpretation layer that ingests MethylForge's candidates.json-compatible findings export."
